1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,520
Before she died,

2
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:04,306
my grandmother made me promise one thing.

3
00:00:04,616 --> 00:00:06,809
Never fix the kitchen tap.

4
00:00:07,119 --> 00:00:09,158
I lasted nine days.

5
00:00:16,908 --> 00:00:20,823
Gran's house stands at the very end of Moor End,

6
00:00:20,873 --> 00:00:22,483
in Thornhallow,

7
00:00:22,533 --> 00:00:24,260
where the road gives up and the moor begins.

8
00:00:24,570 --> 00:00:25,850
Stone walls.

9
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,580
A slate roof that leaks in one corner.

10
00:00:28,630 --> 00:00:30,730
A garden that's mostly nettles,

11
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,625
apart from the roses.

12
00:00:32,934 --> 00:00:35,574
She grew them in a ring at the bottom of the garden.

13
00:00:35,624 --> 00:00:36,754
Red ones.

14
00:00:36,804 --> 00:00:38,634
They flowered in December.

15
00:00:38,684 --> 00:00:40,783
Nobody ever asked her how.

16
00:00:41,093 --> 00:00:43,908
I spent every summer in that house as a boy.

17
00:00:43,958 --> 00:00:45,273
Mum worked,

18
00:00:45,323 --> 00:00:47,717
and Gran didn't mind having me.

19
00:00:48,026 --> 00:00:49,616
She was strict about very little.

20
00:00:49,666 --> 00:00:51,256
Shoes off at the door.

21
00:00:51,306 --> 00:00:53,279
Grace before tea.

22
00:00:53,590 --> 00:00:54,837
And the tap.

23
00:00:55,387 --> 00:00:57,282
Every night,

24
00:00:57,332 --> 00:01:00,057
at eleven o'clock,

25
00:01:00,107 --> 00:01:02,057
she'd go into the kitchen in her dressing gown,

26
00:01:02,107 --> 00:01:02,787
take hold of the cold tap,

27
00:01:02,837 --> 00:01:04,053
and give it a quarter turn.

28
00:01:04,363 --> 00:01:05,213
Not a half.

29
00:01:05,263 --> 00:01:06,553
Not a full turn.

30
00:01:06,603 --> 00:01:07,713
A quarter.

31
00:01:08,583 --> 00:01:09,818
Then she'd stand there,

32
00:01:09,868 --> 00:01:10,928
very still,

33
00:01:10,978 --> 00:01:12,608
until it started to drip.

34
00:01:12,658 --> 00:01:13,668
One drop,

35
00:01:13,718 --> 00:01:15,190
every two seconds.

36
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:18,118
Only then would she go up to bed.

37
00:01:18,428 --> 00:01:21,878
I asked her once why she didn't just get it fixed.

38
00:01:22,188 --> 00:01:23,245
She said,

39
00:01:24,115 --> 00:01:25,535
Some things want fixing.

40
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:27,448
Some things want watching.

41
00:01:27,838 --> 00:01:28,728
I was eight.

42
00:01:28,778 --> 00:01:30,541
I didn't understand.

43
00:01:31,251 --> 00:01:33,856
There was one room I was never allowed in.

44
00:01:33,906 --> 00:01:34,646
The back bedroom,

45
00:01:34,696 --> 00:01:36,761
at the top of the stairs.

46
00:01:36,811 --> 00:01:38,502
It was always locked.

47
00:01:38,812 --> 00:01:41,112
She said it was full of Grandad's things,

48
00:01:41,162 --> 00:01:42,836
and she couldn't face them.

49
00:01:43,146 --> 00:01:46,971
Grandad walked out on her in the winter of nineteen seventy-four.

50
00:01:47,021 --> 00:01:48,141
He took nothing.

51
00:01:48,191 --> 00:01:49,636
He left no note.

52
00:01:49,686 --> 00:01:51,816
Nobody ever saw him again.

53
00:01:52,126 --> 00:01:53,461
She never remarried.

54
00:01:53,511 --> 00:01:55,691
She never even took off her ring.

55
00:01:56,001 --> 00:01:57,906
Everyone said I had her eyes.

56
00:01:57,956 --> 00:01:58,791
Grey,

57
00:01:58,841 --> 00:02:00,700
like the moor in the rain.

58
00:02:01,009 --> 00:02:02,809
Gran died in October.

59
00:02:02,859 --> 00:02:04,500
She was eighty-six.

60
00:02:04,811 --> 00:02:07,466
The last time I saw her,

61
00:02:07,516 --> 00:02:08,771
in the hospital,

62
00:02:08,821 --> 00:02:11,150
she took my wrist and held it so hard it bruised.

63
00:02:11,459 --> 00:02:13,760
Promise me you won't fix that tap.

64
00:02:14,150 --> 00:02:15,145
I promised.

65
00:02:15,195 --> 00:02:17,234
I'd have promised her anything.

66
00:02:18,104 --> 00:02:19,758
She left me the house.

67
00:02:23,908 --> 00:02:26,826
I moved in the week after the funeral.

68
00:02:27,135 --> 00:02:28,960
The house still smelt of her.

69
00:02:29,010 --> 00:02:29,940
Lavender,

70
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:31,245
coal tar soap,

71
00:02:31,295 --> 00:02:32,800
and something underneath it,

72
00:02:32,850 --> 00:02:34,802
like a cellar after rain.

73
00:02:35,113 --> 00:02:36,283
On the first night,

74
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:38,363
I'd forgotten all about the tap,

75
00:02:38,413 --> 00:02:40,458
until I was lying in bed.

76
00:02:45,807 --> 00:02:47,052
It's a small sound,

77
00:02:47,102 --> 00:02:48,047
in daylight.

78
00:02:48,097 --> 00:02:49,947
At night,

79
00:02:49,997 --> 00:02:50,722
in an empty house,

80
00:02:50,772 --> 00:02:51,786
it fills every room.

81
00:02:52,096 --> 00:02:53,476
I'd lie there counting.

82
00:02:53,526 --> 00:02:54,621
I couldn't stop.

83
00:02:54,671 --> 00:02:56,261
Seven hundred drops.

84
00:02:56,311 --> 00:02:57,429
Eight hundred.

85
00:02:57,739 --> 00:02:58,824
By the third night,

86
00:02:58,874 --> 00:03:01,799
I was sleeping with a pillow over my head.

87
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:02,945
By the fifth,

88
00:03:02,995 --> 00:03:05,171
I'd started to notice something.

89
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:07,342
The drip wasn't steady.

90
00:03:09,012 --> 00:03:10,217
On dark nights,

91
00:03:10,267 --> 00:03:13,537
when there was no moon over the garden,

92
00:03:13,587 --> 00:03:14,632
it came faster.

93
00:03:14,682 --> 00:03:15,841
As if the tap was nervous.

94
00:03:16,151 --> 00:03:17,276
On bright nights,

95
00:03:17,326 --> 00:03:19,170
it slowed right down.

96
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:21,250
I told myself it was the pressure.

97
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:22,480
Old pipes.

98
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:23,962
Cold weather.

99
00:03:24,272 --> 00:03:26,467
And once,

100
00:03:26,517 --> 00:03:28,292
around four in the morning,

101
00:03:28,342 --> 00:03:30,857
I looked out of the back window,

102
00:03:30,907 --> 00:03:32,117
and there was frost on the whole garden.

103
00:03:32,167 --> 00:03:33,516
Everywhere except the rose bed.

104
00:03:35,187 --> 00:03:37,232
On the seventh day,

105
00:03:37,282 --> 00:03:37,832
I met the man next door.

106
00:03:37,882 --> 00:03:39,067
Mr Haworth.

107
00:03:39,117 --> 00:03:39,882
Ninety,

108
00:03:39,932 --> 00:03:41,185
if he was a day.

109
00:03:41,495 --> 00:03:44,245
He watched me carrying bin bags down the path,

110
00:03:44,295 --> 00:03:45,210
and said,

111
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,755
you'll be keeping the water going, then.

112
00:03:48,065 --> 00:03:49,416
I said, sorry?

113
00:03:49,966 --> 00:03:51,316
He said,

114
00:03:51,366 --> 00:03:51,911
your gran.

115
00:03:51,961 --> 00:03:52,986
She kept the water moving.

116
00:03:53,036 --> 00:03:53,931
Every night.

117
00:03:53,981 --> 00:03:55,677
Fifty-odd years.

118
00:03:55,987 --> 00:03:57,664
I asked him what for.

119
00:03:57,974 --> 00:03:59,124
He looked past me,

120
00:03:59,174 --> 00:04:00,219
down the garden,

121
00:04:00,269 --> 00:04:01,394
at the roses.

122
00:04:01,444 --> 00:04:04,267
Then he went inside and shut his door.

123
00:04:04,576 --> 00:04:06,301
That night,

124
00:04:06,351 --> 00:04:07,486
I tried the back bedroom.

125
00:04:07,536 --> 00:04:09,696
Still locked.

126
00:04:09,746 --> 00:04:10,836
I searched the whole house for the key.

127
00:04:10,886 --> 00:04:11,796
Every drawer.

128
00:04:11,846 --> 00:04:12,666
Every tin.

129
00:04:12,716 --> 00:04:13,497
Every coat pocket.

130
00:04:13,807 --> 00:04:14,830
Nothing.

131
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:16,615
By the ninth day,

132
00:04:16,665 --> 00:04:19,335
I hadn't slept properly in over a week.

133
00:04:19,385 --> 00:04:22,084
I was counting drops in my dreams.

134
00:04:22,394 --> 00:04:23,139
And I thought,

135
00:04:23,189 --> 00:04:24,049
she's gone.

136
00:04:24,099 --> 00:04:25,109
It's a tap.

137
00:04:25,159 --> 00:04:27,902
It's a washer that costs forty pence.

138
00:04:28,212 --> 00:04:30,100
So I rang a plumber.

139
00:04:34,250 --> 00:04:35,020
He was young,

140
00:04:35,070 --> 00:04:35,965
and cheerful,

141
00:04:36,015 --> 00:04:37,440
and called Kieran.

142
00:04:37,490 --> 00:04:40,887
He had a van with a cartoon spanner on the side.

143
00:04:41,197 --> 00:04:42,517
He took one look at the tap and laughed.

144
00:04:42,567 --> 00:04:43,397
Your gran's been doing this on purpose,

145
00:04:43,447 --> 00:04:46,627
he said.

146
00:04:46,677 --> 00:04:48,067
Washer's fine.

147
00:04:48,117 --> 00:04:50,594
It's just been opened a quarter turn.

148
00:04:50,904 --> 00:04:53,244
Then he crouched under the sink with his torch,

149
00:04:53,294 --> 00:04:54,749
and went quiet.

150
00:04:55,059 --> 00:04:55,904
That's odd,

151
00:04:55,954 --> 00:04:56,815
he said.

152
00:04:57,365 --> 00:04:59,960
The cold pipe didn't go where it should.

153
00:05:00,010 --> 00:05:02,266
It didn't go down to the mains.

154
00:05:02,575 --> 00:05:03,855
It went sideways.

155
00:05:03,905 --> 00:05:05,235
Through the back wall.

156
00:05:05,285 --> 00:05:07,037
Out into the garden.

157
00:05:07,347 --> 00:05:08,987
We followed it with a spade.

158
00:05:09,037 --> 00:05:10,972
It ran a foot under the lawn,

159
00:05:11,022 --> 00:05:11,912
in a long,

160
00:05:11,962 --> 00:05:13,321
careful curve.

161
00:05:13,631 --> 00:05:15,899
All the way round the rose bed.

162
00:05:16,209 --> 00:05:17,649
And back into the house,

163
00:05:17,699 --> 00:05:19,741
to the drain under the sink.

164
00:05:20,052 --> 00:05:21,580
A complete circle.

165
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:25,540
Kieran stood up and scratched his head.

166
00:05:25,590 --> 00:05:29,335
Somebody's built a ring of running water round your roses,

167
00:05:29,385 --> 00:05:30,115
he said.

168
00:05:30,165 --> 00:05:31,320
Like a moat.

169
00:05:31,370 --> 00:05:33,517
Never seen anything like it.

170
00:05:33,827 --> 00:05:35,042
He said it was old.

171
00:05:35,092 --> 00:05:35,857
Copper.

172
00:05:35,907 --> 00:05:36,812
Seventies,

173
00:05:36,862 --> 00:05:38,606
by the look of the joints.

174
00:05:38,916 --> 00:05:41,046
Nineteen seventy-four, I thought.

175
00:05:41,096 --> 00:05:42,783
And I didn't know why.

176
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:45,346
He asked me what I wanted done.

177
00:05:45,656 --> 00:05:46,576
I should have said,

178
00:05:46,626 --> 00:05:47,653
leave it.

179
00:05:47,963 --> 00:05:48,703
I said,

180
00:05:48,753 --> 00:05:50,585
can you just make it stop.

181
00:05:50,895 --> 00:05:52,330
He capped the pipe at the wall.

182
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:53,325
Ten minutes.

183
00:05:53,375 --> 00:05:54,770
Thirty quid.

184
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:57,040
And the house went quiet.

185
00:06:01,590 --> 00:06:03,880
For the first time in fifty-two years,

186
00:06:03,930 --> 00:06:06,195
nothing in that kitchen moved.

187
00:06:06,505 --> 00:06:08,355
I stood there for a long time,

188
00:06:08,405 --> 00:06:10,324
listening to the silence.

189
00:06:10,634 --> 00:06:13,353
I remember thinking how peaceful it was.

190
00:06:17,503 --> 00:06:19,358
That night, I slept like the dead.

191
00:06:19,408 --> 00:06:20,063
Deep,

192
00:06:20,113 --> 00:06:20,963
and black,

193
00:06:21,013 --> 00:06:22,254
and dreamless.

194
00:06:22,564 --> 00:06:23,834
I woke at three.

195
00:06:23,884 --> 00:06:25,422
I didn't know why.

196
00:06:25,733 --> 00:06:27,172
Then I did.

197
00:06:28,041 --> 00:06:29,221
There was no drip.

198
00:06:29,271 --> 00:06:31,261
There would never be a drip again.

199
00:06:31,311 --> 00:06:32,886
And somewhere in the house,

200
00:06:32,936 --> 00:06:35,224
something else had taken its place.

201
00:06:35,535 --> 00:06:37,130
A sound, downstairs.

202
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:38,625
Slow. Heavy.

203
00:06:38,675 --> 00:06:41,722
Like someone stamping the mud off their boots.

204
00:06:42,032 --> 00:06:44,455
I went down with my phone torch.

205
00:06:44,765 --> 00:06:46,195
The back door was shut.

206
00:06:46,245 --> 00:06:47,025
Locked.

207
00:06:47,075 --> 00:06:48,537
The key on its hook.

208
00:06:48,848 --> 00:06:51,634
But there was soil on the kitchen floor.

209
00:06:51,944 --> 00:06:52,229
Wet,

210
00:06:52,279 --> 00:06:53,104
dark soil.

211
00:06:53,154 --> 00:06:54,359
And rose petals.

212
00:06:54,409 --> 00:06:55,586
Red ones.

213
00:06:55,896 --> 00:06:57,676
It smelt of the rose bed.

214
00:06:57,726 --> 00:06:58,701
Turned earth,

215
00:06:58,751 --> 00:07:00,611
and something sweet underneath it,

216
00:07:00,661 --> 00:07:02,662
like fruit left too long.

217
00:07:03,371 --> 00:07:04,286
A trail of it,

218
00:07:04,336 --> 00:07:05,496
from the back door,

219
00:07:05,546 --> 00:07:06,811
across the kitchen,

220
00:07:06,861 --> 00:07:08,918
to the bottom of the stairs.

221
00:07:09,229 --> 00:07:10,507
And up them.

222
00:07:11,858 --> 00:07:14,013
I followed it,

223
00:07:14,063 --> 00:07:15,918
one stair at a time.

224
00:07:15,968 --> 00:07:17,443
Every step had a print on it.

225
00:07:17,493 --> 00:07:18,758
A man's boot.

226
00:07:18,808 --> 00:07:19,508
An old-fashioned heel.

227
00:07:19,818 --> 00:07:22,181
It stopped at the top of the stairs.

228
00:07:22,491 --> 00:07:24,061
At the back bedroom.

229
00:07:24,611 --> 00:07:26,299
The door was open.

230
00:07:27,809 --> 00:07:29,469
Fifty-two years locked,

231
00:07:29,519 --> 00:07:31,144
and now it stood open,

232
00:07:31,194 --> 00:07:32,189
just a crack,

233
00:07:32,239 --> 00:07:34,793
and cold air was coming out of it.

234
00:07:35,102 --> 00:07:36,438
I pushed it.

235
00:07:38,268 --> 00:07:39,013
Inside,

236
00:07:39,063 --> 00:07:41,355
it was nineteen seventy-four.

237
00:07:43,186 --> 00:07:44,561
A brown armchair.

238
00:07:44,611 --> 00:07:46,246
A calendar on the wall,

239
00:07:46,296 --> 00:07:47,726
turned to December.

240
00:07:47,776 --> 00:07:50,271
A man's coat laid out on the bed,

241
00:07:50,321 --> 00:07:52,712
as if he'd only just taken it off.

242
00:07:53,022 --> 00:07:55,537
A wedding photo on the bedside table.

243
00:07:55,587 --> 00:07:56,467
Gran,

244
00:07:56,517 --> 00:07:57,817
young, laughing.

245
00:07:57,867 --> 00:07:58,907
And next to her,

246
00:07:58,957 --> 00:08:00,542
a man in a dark suit,

247
00:08:00,592 --> 00:08:01,897
with my nose,

248
00:08:01,947 --> 00:08:02,720
and my chin.

249
00:08:03,029 --> 00:08:04,544
The bed was dented.

250
00:08:04,594 --> 00:08:07,121
As if someone had been sitting on it.

251
00:08:07,431 --> 00:08:08,386
And on the pillow,

252
00:08:08,436 --> 00:08:09,531
there was a letter.

253
00:08:09,581 --> 00:08:11,747
In Gran's handwriting.

254
00:08:12,057 --> 00:08:13,072
On the envelope,

255
00:08:13,122 --> 00:08:14,304
one word.

256
00:08:14,614 --> 00:08:15,704
My name.

257
00:08:19,854 --> 00:08:21,594
If you're reading this,

258
00:08:21,644 --> 00:08:21,899
you fixed the tap.

259
00:08:21,949 --> 00:08:23,519
Don't be cross with yourself.

260
00:08:23,569 --> 00:08:24,854
I always knew you would.

261
00:08:24,904 --> 00:08:26,863
You never could leave a thing alone.

262
00:08:27,252 --> 00:08:29,717
I'm sorry I lied to you about your grandad.

263
00:08:29,767 --> 00:08:31,318
He didn't walk out.

264
00:08:31,709 --> 00:08:35,264
In the winter of seventy-four, he came home late across the moor.

265
00:08:35,314 --> 00:08:37,074
Something had followed him.

266
00:08:37,124 --> 00:08:40,078
By the next night, he wasn't your grandad any more.

267
00:08:40,468 --> 00:08:41,873
I did what had to be done.

268
00:08:41,923 --> 00:08:43,523
I put him in the garden.

269
00:08:43,573 --> 00:08:46,283
I planted roses over him.

270
00:08:46,333 --> 00:08:47,373
And I laid the pipe myself.

271
00:08:47,763 --> 00:08:49,178
Running water, love.

272
00:08:49,228 --> 00:08:51,378
It's the one thing they cannot cross.

273
00:08:51,428 --> 00:08:54,243
As long as the water moved, he couldn't rise.

274
00:08:54,633 --> 00:08:57,334
So every night, I gave it a quarter turn.

275
00:08:57,724 --> 00:09:00,232
Fifty-two years of quarter turns.

276
00:09:00,622 --> 00:09:03,032
I'm not sorry. But I'm so tired.

277
00:09:03,422 --> 00:09:05,342
If the water's stopped, he'll come home.

278
00:09:05,392 --> 00:09:06,717
He'll go to his room.

279
00:09:06,767 --> 00:09:09,397
He'll think it's still nineteen seventy-four.

280
00:09:09,787 --> 00:09:11,603
And then, he'll look for me.

281
00:09:11,993 --> 00:09:13,993
Don't let him see your face.

282
00:09:14,383 --> 00:09:16,125
You look just like me.

283
00:09:18,675 --> 00:09:19,960
I read it twice.

284
00:09:20,010 --> 00:09:21,259
Then I ran.

285
00:09:21,569 --> 00:09:22,639
Down the stairs.

286
00:09:22,689 --> 00:09:23,829
Into the kitchen.

287
00:09:23,879 --> 00:09:25,137
To the tap.

288
00:09:25,447 --> 00:09:26,647
I took hold of it,

289
00:09:26,697 --> 00:09:28,367
the way she always did,

290
00:09:28,417 --> 00:09:30,547
and I gave it a quarter turn.

291
00:09:30,857 --> 00:09:31,880
Nothing.

292
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:33,650
Another.

293
00:09:34,201 --> 00:09:34,806
Nothing.

294
00:09:34,856 --> 00:09:35,751
Not a drop.

295
00:09:35,801 --> 00:09:38,058
Kieran had capped it at the wall.

296
00:09:38,367 --> 00:09:39,327
And behind me,

297
00:09:39,377 --> 00:09:40,847
at the top of the stairs,

298
00:09:40,897 --> 00:09:42,348
a door opened.

299
00:09:42,659 --> 00:09:43,899
Footsteps. Slow.

300
00:09:43,949 --> 00:09:44,439
Heavy.

301
00:09:44,489 --> 00:09:45,676
Coming down.

302
00:09:45,986 --> 00:09:47,241
I stood in the dark,

303
00:09:47,291 --> 00:09:49,321
with my hand on a dry tap,

304
00:09:49,371 --> 00:09:51,289
and I didn't turn around.

305
00:09:51,598 --> 00:09:52,883
The footsteps stopped,

306
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:54,455
right behind me.

307
00:09:54,766 --> 00:09:56,536
And a voice I'd never heard,

308
00:09:56,586 --> 00:09:57,501
in a house I'd known all my life,

309
00:09:57,551 --> 00:09:59,653
said,

310
00:10:00,523 --> 00:10:01,313
Margaret?

311
00:10:01,363 --> 00:10:02,746
I'm home.
